WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:07.620
So listen, there are people who would feel
a sense of satisfaction from what I'm about

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.950
to play for you.

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.460
I feel no satisfaction whatsoever.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:18.130
I actually feel despair when I see the video
I'm about to play for you because it's emblematic

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:21.880
of so much of what's wrong with our country.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:30.189
This is an example of yet again, another Republican
who was very laissez faire, about covid and

00:00:30.189 --> 00:00:36.520
stood behind Trump literally and figuratively,
with no mask, defending everything Trump was

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:41.500
doing, praising Trump until he got Coronavirus
himself.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:47.770
And I'm talking about former New Jersey Republican
Governor Chris Christie, who ended up after

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:51.510
not wearing a mask at the White House at a
super spreader event.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:56.640
Chris Christie ended up in a hospital, ICU
with covid.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:04.580
And now Chris Christie is in a national ad
defiantly and powerfully advocating for mask

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:05.580
wearing.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.580
So take a look at the.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:12.990
And here is Chris Christie specifically with
a message to those refusing to wear a mask.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:14.979
This message isn't for everyone.

00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:19.899
It's for all those people who refuse to wear
a mask, you know, lying in isolation in ICU

00:01:19.899 --> 00:01:20.899
for seven days.

00:01:20.899 --> 00:01:24.649
I thought about how wrong I was to remove
my mask at the White House today.

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:30.499
I think about how wrong it is to mask wearing,
divide us, especially as we now know you're

00:01:30.499 --> 00:01:36.810
twice as likely to get covid-19 if you don't
wear a mask, because if you don't do the right

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:40.880
thing, we could all end up on the wrong side
of history.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.939
Please wear a mask.

00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:48.750
So Chris Christie says, as we now know, but
we've known this for months.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.159
So, OK, it's true.

00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:56.749
We may be didn't know in February and March
about masks, but Chris Christie got covid

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:58.119
a couple of months ago.

00:01:58.119 --> 00:02:04.039
We knew for six months at that point about
the importance of wearing masks and not doing

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:08.780
indoor events, everything that Chris Christie
participated in, which likely got him the

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:09.780
virus.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.020
So I get it.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.970
On the one hand, good for Chris Christie.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:17.320
And I see lots of leftest retweeting this
ad on Twitter.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:23.790
OK, but this goes back to one of the real
tragedies of the Republican Party and reactionary

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.500
right wing thinking in the United States.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.500
This is not new.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:29.890
If you've been watching the show, listening
for a while, you've heard me say this before.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:35.560
His view changed only because he got the virus
and he may only be willing to do this ad because

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:39.420
ultimately Donald Trump already lost and he
knows that there's less of a political risk

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.530
to doing it.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:46.370
This is just like the homophobic Republican
who spends 20 years fighting against gay rights

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:49.300
and then finds out their kid is gay and has
an awakening.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:54.390
OK, it's great when someone comes around to
the correct position, there is no doubt about

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.390
it.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:02.080
But why does it have to happen only when you
recognize that it affects you personally.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.930
It only happens when you have a kid or what?

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:06.930
Right.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.070
We've talked about the homophobic example.

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:14.820
Can't you simply empathize with the parent
of the gay kid who sees you fighting against

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:17.790
gay rights and have that same awakening?

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:21.540
Couldn't Chris Christie have understood the
importance of mask's without ending up in

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.740
the ICU personally after taking his mask off
at the White House?

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:33.770
Why does it take being in an ICU with coronavirus
to understand what we should be doing?

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:40.450
Do you think that there's something physiological
going on where some of us are able to say,

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.450
hey, you know what?

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.240
I didn't have covered that that I know of.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.200
In fact, maybe I did actually back back in
April.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.330
But that's a different story.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.200
I'm not aware that I certainly had it.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:56.850
And if I did, I didn't end up in the ICU,
but I still wear a mask and don't do indoor

00:03:56.850 --> 00:04:00.770
gatherings and so on and so forth, because
I understand that even if it didn't happen

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:03.450
to me, it's happening to other people.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:07.030
Why is it that the Republicans seem unable
to do it?

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.100
I don't know the answer.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.920
I'm genuinely asking it.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:17.019
When we see a Republican show, a shred of
humanity and empathy, it's because they or

00:04:17.019 --> 00:04:19.660
someone in their family had something happen
to them.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:22.030
And until that point, they don't seem to care.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.260
Chris Christie is absolutely correct.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:28.940
And if this video that he did, if this ad
he did convinces someone to wear a mask who

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:35.620
hasn't been all power to Chris Christie, but
this is pathetic that this is what it took

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:40.930
for him to come to this conclusion if he's
pushing deniers to act responsibly.

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:42.710
Thank you, Chris.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:43.710
Fantastic.

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:48.330
But why did it take until almost a year into
the pandemic if we had had more prominent

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:53.340
Republicans saying these things in March instead
of 15 cases will soon be zero?

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.430
It's like a flu.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.130
We're handling it perfectly.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:58.090
We would be much better off right now.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:01.540
I prefer public servants.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:08.470
Who can see beyond how something affects them
personally and understand how things affect

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:11.770
other people and society at large?

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:16.690
So, yeah, I know that there are leftists who
are merely praising Chris Christie, and that's

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.350
fine and it's fine to amplify the message.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:21.160
But this is a microcosm.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:30.150
This is emblematic of the lack of or inability
to experience empathy that seems to be an

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:33.460
epidemic in and of itself among the American
right.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:37.140
